+    An item of the list can also be a ``(path, priority)`` tuple to
+    control the search order independently of the order the paths are
+    given in. Paths with a higher priority are searched first. Paths
+    with the same priority are searched in the order they were given,
+    and a path without an explicit priority has priority ``0``. Regular
+    paths and tuples can be mixed, and priorities may be negative.
+
+    .. code-block:: python
+
+        loader = FileSystemLoader([
+            ("/high/priority/themes", 100),  # searched first
+            ("/medium/priority/plugins", 50),  # searched second
+            "/default/templates",  # priority 0, searched third
+            ("/low/priority/fallback", -10),  # searched last
+        ])
+
+    The paths that were resolved to a template are remembered, so
+    loading the same template name again does not search every
